          "id": "d901cf98da94c7225276af45d755ae8eed6db34f",
          "message": "fix(operations): protect a merge's seam only on doubled-seam evidence (#203)\n\nThe seam guard added to `unify_faces` for a wall split at its seam fell\nback to the surface frame's `u = 0` meridian when no face in the merge\ngroup used a seam line twice. An ordinary section generator that happens\nto lie on that meridian was then protected instead of removed: three\noverlapping cylinders in a row kept their lens generators, and every\nmerged wall came back with a bogus inner wire and an open mesh (78\nboundary edges at spacing 9), which OpenZCAD's unify guard declined —\nits overlapping-pattern unions regressed from 6 faces to 13.\n\nOnly a doubled seam line in the group is evidence of a seam now; without\none, no shared edge is protected, which is the behaviour before the\nguard. The seam-split wall the guard was written for still carries its\nupper seam piece twice, so it is unaffected.\n\nSigned-off-by: Peter <171875562+petertoday@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
