          "distinct": true,
          "id": "1799e12a8d1480c4f58eab1242dbaba7402dab4f",
          "message": "fix(operations): judge a blend postcondition at the part's own scale (#204)\n\nThe fail-closed blend postcondition validates its result with the\nchecker's default options, whose geometric tolerance is an absolute\n1e-6. On a part with features under a few microns the wire\nself-intersection check then reads every pair of non-adjacent edges as\ntouching: a 2 µm box with a 0.3 µm fillet on its verticals — sixteen\nvertices exactly where they belong — was reported \"self-intersecting\"\nat precisely the fillet chord, 0.42 µm, and the fillet was refused.\nBefore the postcondition existed the same call succeeded, so OpenZCAD's\nmicron-scale vertex-identity fixture stopped building on the kernel\nbump.\n\nThe postcondition and its input baseline now share options whose\ntolerance scale follows the input solid's shortest edge: 1 at 10 µm\nand above, so ordinary parts are judged exactly as before, and never\nbelow 1e-2 so a degenerate input edge cannot switch the check off.\n\nSigned-off-by: Peter <171875562+petertoday@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-09-02T20:41:31-04:00",
