          "id": "cc1c0fd0609da6a2b2925e719b156db787b7111f",
          "message": "ci: activate the v3 fleet callees with job timeouts and the cargo-fuzz pin (#1185)\n\n## Change\n\nActivates the `-v3` reusable workflows staged in #1183, following the\nsame pattern as #1179 → #1170.\n\n- **Manifest.** `.github/fleet-workflows.json` now selects\n`fleet-{ci,fuzz,osv,wasm-candidate,wasm-size}-v3.yml`. Benchmark,\ngauntlet, mutants-sharded and mutation-scope stay on `-v2`.\n- **Pins.** The callers `ci.yml` (`checks` and `wasm-size`), `fuzz.yml`,\n`osv-scan.yml` and `openzcad-wasm-release.yml` are pinned to\n`59d02a10f498a2b3c24512e8b2d9ba8150bbdb1e`, the squash commit of #1183\non main. Each pinned callee is byte-identical to the checked-in file.\n- **Retired files.** The five replaced `-v2` callees are deleted.\n- **Behaviour change.** Every previously unbounded job in those five\nworkflows now has `timeout-minutes`. Coverage gets 180 min, WASM build\n60, WASM candidate 60, and smaller jobs 5–30, roughly 3× the observed\nhosted durations. The fuzz preparation step installs `cargo-fuzz\n--version 0.13.2`. Commands, guards, permissions, runner selection and\njob/check names are unchanged, so `checks / CI Pass` keeps its name.\n- **Tests.** `scripts/test_fleet_workflows.py` now reads the landed v2\nbytes from git at `e07ae8e` instead of the deleted files. Each v3 file\nmust differ from them only by the job timeouts and the cargo-fuzz pin.\nv3 is accepted as an active and main-manifest version.\n- **Docs.** References in `docs/owner-pr-ci.md` and a comment in\n`ci.yml` now say `fleet-ci-v3.yml`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `python3 scripts/test_fleet_workflows.py`: 10 tests pass. Negative\ncontrol: changing a fuzz command in `fleet-fuzz-v3.yml` is rejected by\nboth the pin check and the v3-delta test.\n- The Repository Policy script set passes locally, including Ubuntu\nrouting, direct fleet, CI convergence, owner-PR routing (which imports\nthe fleet-workflow tests), gauntlet contract and doc paths/module map.\nThe privacy suite and commit-metadata check also pass.\n- `actionlint` 1.7.12 reports no findings.\n- **Not run locally:** `test-mutants-scope.py` needs cargo-mutants, and\n`taplo fmt --check` needs taplo; no TOML changed.\n\n## Compatibility and risks\n\n- **Files deleted:**\n`fleet-{ci,fuzz,osv,wasm-candidate,wasm-size}-v2.yml`. Nothing\nreferences them after this change; the old pins at `e07ae8e` keep\nresolving for historical runs.\n- **Self-hosted fleet:** `docs/owner-pr-ci.md` requires the trusted\nrunner group to allow the exact immutable `fleet-ci` revision. Fleet\nrouting is currently disabled (jobs run hosted), so nothing changes\ntoday. Before enabling `CI_FLEET_ENABLED`, the runner group needs an\nentry for `fleet-ci-v3.yml@59d02a1`.\n- A job that legitimately runs past its new limit now fails instead of\nrunning up to 360 min. The limits were set from hosted run times; the\nlegacy 1-CPU fleet profile would be slower.\n\n## WASM module tier\n\nNone.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01RAFdKbytobmE6B5tmrSS1Z)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
