          "id": "a05f0d2fbf413d168aacd3653b12870e650b87d3",
          "message": "ci: stage callees with current comments and the caller-owned gauntlet tier (#1195)\n\n## Change\n\nPinned reusable workflows can't be edited in place. So the leftover\nstale comments from the CI review are staged here as new versions, to be\nswitched on by a follow-up activation PR (the same pattern as #1183 →\n#1185). Nothing calls these files yet; the active callees and their pins\nare unchanged.\n\n- **`fleet-wasm-size-v4.yml`**: the comment names the gate's callee\nthrough `.github/fleet-workflows.json` instead of the retired\n`fleet-ci.yml` filename.\n- **`fleet-osv-v4.yml`**: adds the missing `# v7.0.1` comment to the\n`actions/checkout` pin.\n- **`fleet-mutants-sharded-v3.yml`**: the comment describes the verdict\nthat landed in #1187. That covers the 8-shard single-wave cap and\nsampling, and the run failing on a non-green baseline, nothing examined,\ntimeouts, mutants left without an outcome by a run that ended before the\nbudget, or unreadable output. Missed mutants are reported, not failed.\n- **`fleet-gauntlet-v3.yml`**: drops the callee's duplicate match on the\nweekly cron. Since #1183, `gauntlet.yml` maps its own `47 3 * * 0`\nschedule to `abc-1k` and passes `tier`, so the callee now reads only its\n`tier` input, which defaults to `smoke`. The callee is\n`workflow_call`-only, so no other trigger relied on the removed branch.\n- **`scripts/test_fleet_workflows.py`**: the v3 timeout test is\nrestricted to the families it covers. The new\n`test_staged_versions_only_refresh_comments_and_the_gauntlet_tier`\nrequires each staged file to equal its active callee once comments are\nstripped, apart from the reviewed gauntlet tier step.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test_fleet_workflows.py`, `test-gauntlet-workflow.py`,\n`test-mutants-verdict.py`, `test-ubuntu-ci-routing.py`,\n`test-direct-fleet.py` and the owner/fleet policy tests pass locally.\n- `actionlint` and `scripts/check-doc-paths.sh` pass.\n- Negative control: changing `contents: read` to `contents: write` in\n`fleet-osv-v4.yml` fails the staging test.\n\n## Compatibility and risks\n\n- New files only; no caller references them until the activation PR.\n- The gauntlet change is behavioural once activated. The Sunday tier\nthen depends only on the caller's mapping, which\n`test-gauntlet-workflow.py` already pins.\n- No change to kernel code, file formats, units, tolerances or\ndependencies.\n\n## WASM module tier\n\nNone.\n\n---\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01RAFdKbytobmE6B5tmrSS1Z)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
