          "distinct": true,
          "id": "71e856d66641b27c84cd422c3b4856d32c2a8353",
          "message": "ci: activate the refreshed wasm-size, osv, mutants and gauntlet callees (#1197)\n\n## Change\n\nThis activates the callees staged in #1195. It follows the same two-step\npattern as #1183 → #1185.\n\n- **Manifest.** `.github/fleet-workflows.json` now selects:\n  - `fleet-wasm-size-v4.yml`\n  - `fleet-osv-v4.yml`\n  - `fleet-mutants-sharded-v3.yml`\n  - `fleet-gauntlet-v3.yml`\n- **Pins.** These callers are pinned to\n`a05f0d2fbf413d168aacd3653b12870e650b87d3`, the commit #1195 landed as\non main:\n  - `ci.yml` (`wasm-size` job)\n  - `osv-scan.yml`\n  - `mutants.yml`\n  - `gauntlet.yml`\n\n  Each pinned callee is byte-identical to the checked-in file.\n- **Retired files.** These four callees are replaced and deleted:\n  - `fleet-wasm-size-v3.yml`\n  - `fleet-osv-v3.yml`\n  - `fleet-mutants-sharded-v2.yml`\n  - `fleet-gauntlet-v2.yml`\n- **Behaviour change.** The gauntlet callee now takes its tier only from\nits `tier` input, defaulting to `smoke`. `gauntlet.yml` already maps its\nweekly `47 3 * * 0` cron to `abc-1k`, so the Sunday run still gets\n`abc-1k`. The other three callees change only in comments.\n- **Path filters.** `mutation-scope.yml` now watches\n`fleet-mutants-sharded-v3.yml` instead of v2. The `mutants.yml` comment\nno longer says the callee's comment is stale, and it lists the\nfinished-run outcome rule.\n- **Tests.**\n- `scripts/test_fleet_workflows.py`: the staging test becomes\n`test_refreshed_callees_only_change_comments_and_the_gauntlet_tier`. It\ncompares each active callee with the file it replaced, read from git at\nthe commit where that file landed. The v3 timeout test reads the\nreplaced v3 files from `59d02a1` the same way. The cross-family delta\ncheck also strips the refresh deltas, and accepts `-v4` as a\nmain-manifest version.\n- `scripts/test-gauntlet-workflow.py`: now requires the callee to use\n`tier=${REQUESTED_TIER:-smoke}` and to contain no schedule check.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Every `python3 scripts/test*` that `fleet-ci-v3.yml` runs passes\nlocally, plus `test-mutants-verdict.py`, `actionlint` and\n`scripts/check-doc-paths.sh`.\n- The four activated files are identical to #1195's head and to\n`a05f0d2f`.\n- Negative controls:\n- Each of these fails the refresh test: changing a permission in\n`fleet-osv-v4.yml`, changing the gauntlet default tier, or changing the\nmutants `max-parallel`.\n- Pinning `mutants.yml` to a commit without the callee fails the pin\ncheck.\n- **Not run locally:** `test-mutants-scope.py` needs cargo-mutants. The\nMutation Scope workflow runs it here, because this PR changes its path\nfilter.\n\n## Compatibility and risks\n\n- **Files deleted:** the four replaced callees. Old immutable pins in\npast runs still resolve from history.\n- **Gauntlet tier:** a direct `workflow_call` of the gauntlet callee\nwithout a `tier` input now runs `smoke` even on Sunday. The only caller,\n`gauntlet.yml`, always passes the mapped tier.\n- No change to kernel code, file formats, units, tolerances or\ndependencies.\n\n## WASM module tier\n\nNone.\n\n---\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01RAFdKbytobmE6B5tmrSS1Z)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
