          "id": "3fd064e7aa7058ea9e575423e4927b163e125ac4",
          "message": "fix(ci): skip unresolvable subject PR numbers when carrying WASM-Size lines (#1210)\n\n## Change\n\n`merged_prs` in `scripts/publish-wasm-package-pr.py` looked up\n`repos/{repo}/pulls/N` for any commit subject that ends in `(#N)`. When\n`#N` has no PR in this repo, for example an upstream-era number, `gh\napi` failed. The `CalledProcessError` then reached `size_section`, which\ndropped the whole span and wrote only the \"Could not collect\" notice.\nThis happened on refresh esaueng/remus#1182 (`pulls/69`) and on\nesaueng/remus#1208 (`pulls/1252`), where the declaration had to be added\nby hand.\n\n`accept` now treats a failed subject lookup as \"not this commit's PR\"\nand returns `False`. The loop then falls through to the existing\n`commits/{sha}/pulls` association lookup. The rule that only a commit's\nown PR settles it is unchanged. A failure in the compare, association or\nprevious-refresh lookups still produces the fail-closed notice.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `python3 scripts/test-package-refresh-pr.py`: 10/10 pass. The new test\nis `test_subject_naming_an_unknown_pr_does_not_abort_collection`. Its\nspan has a commit whose subject names an unknown `(#69)`, so the fake\n`gh` returns 404; that commit's own PR is found through its association.\nA second commit's PR declares a `WASM-Size:` line. The test asserts that\nboth declarations are carried and that the size gate passes. It fails on\n`main` without the fix.\n- `./scripts/check-doc-paths.sh`: OK.\n\n## Compatibility and risks\n\nNone. Only the CI publisher script and its test change.\n\n- esaueng/remus#1204 edits the same script (it adds `close_superseded`),\nbut in a different function. Whichever PR lands second needs a rebase.\n- The \"Collection is fragile\" bullet in\n`.claude/skills/release-flow/SKILL.md` exists only on\nesaueng/remus#1209, which is still open. It is not softened here and\nshould be updated once both PRs have landed.\n\n## WASM module tier\n\nNone.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01SSNnmz4og7GEBVFvSzqDcR)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
