          "id": "86035abca4d2f494003aa71d9c65ac3afdbf8fde",
          "message": "ci: activate fleet-ci-v4 so fuzz compile and render run in tier 1 (#1212)\n\n## Change\n\nThis activates the callee staged in esaueng/remus#1204 (landed as\n`9e5b65b`), the second half of the usual stage/activate pair. Since\n#1204, a merge group runs only tier 1 unless its diff touches a tier-2\ninput. Fuzz Targets Compile and Software Rendering both build against\nmost kernel crates, and Codex flagged both on #1204. With v4 active,\nthey run for every source change, so a kernel change that breaks either\none fails in the queue and never reaches `main`.\n\n- **Manifest and pin.**\n  - `.github/fleet-workflows.json` now selects `fleet-ci-v4.yml`.\n- `ci.yml` calls\n`fleet-ci-v4.yml@9e5b65b9e00f004d83eb583ab3934c863ad7956d`, which is\n#1204's squash commit on `main`; the bytes there are identical to this\nfile.\n- `fleet-ci-v3.yml` is retired. Existing immutable callers can still\nresolve it at its landing commit.\n- **v4 vs v3**, reviewed and pinned in #1204:\n- `fuzz-check` and `render` are selected by `heavy`, no longer by\n`full`.\n- `CI Pass` no longer accepts a skip of either job when `heavy` is true.\n- **Classifier.** `fuzz/` and `crates/render/` no longer keep the second\ntier for a merge group, since both jobs already run with the first. The\nother second-tier inputs are unchanged: Cargo manifests and lock,\ntoolchain, deny/clippy config, `.cargo/`, `.config/`,\n`.github/workflows/`, and committed packages.\n- **Tests follow the active callee.**\n  - `test-ci-convergence.py`: tier 1 gains `fuzz-check` and `render`.\n  - `test-owner-pr-routing.py`: `fuzz-check` is selected by `heavy`.\n- `test_fleet_workflows.py`: reads the retired v3 from its landing\ncommit, and compares the active v4 to the v2 lineage with the reviewed\ntier move undone.\n- `test-classify-ci-changes.py`: covers fuzz and render sources staying\non the queue tier.\n- **Docs.** `docs/owner-pr-ci.md` \"Tiers\" now lists fuzz and render\nunder tier 1.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Local runs pass:\n- `test_fleet_workflows.py`, which includes the pin check:\n`fleet_workflows.py` validates all 9 immutable main-ancestor calls, and\nv4 matches `9e5b65b`;\n- `test-ci-convergence.py`, `test-owner-pr-routing.py`,\n`test-classify-ci-changes.py` (also with\n`GITHUB_EVENT_NAME=merge_group`);\n- the fleet runner, selector and owner policy tests,\n`test-gauntlet-workflow.py`, `test-mutants-verdict.py`,\n`test-package-refresh-pr.py`, `test-publish-credentials.sh`;\n- `check-doc-paths.sh`, `check-doc-module-map.py`,\n`check_public_commit_metadata.py`.\n- `test-direct-fleet.py` and `test-ubuntu-ci-routing.py` fail\nidentically on unmodified `main` in this shallow clone, because a pinned\nguard commit is missing locally. They passed in CI's full clone on\n#1204.\n- This PR's own CI runs the old v3 callee, which is pinned on `main`; v4\ntakes over for PRs and merge groups after this merges. Its merge group\nruns the full suite, because the diff touches `.github/workflows/`.\n\n## Compatibility and risks\n\n- **Every source PR now runs two more jobs:** Fuzz Targets Compile\n(about 30 s of checking plus setup) and Software Rendering (about 1 min\nof tests plus the lavapipe install). That adds hosted-runner load.\n- **Deletes `fleet-ci-v3.yml`**, following the retirement convention in\n`docs/owner-pr-ci.md`.\n- **Self-hosted fleet:** the runner-group allowlist needs\n`fleet-ci-v4.yml@9e5b65b` before `CI_FLEET_ENABLED` is turned on. The\nfleet is off today.\n- No public API, format or dependency changes.\n\n## WASM module tier\n\nNone. No Rust changed.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01BvYiTQJWWBACfhhuFhkAxd)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
