          "message": "docs(skills): catch the pr-workflow and release-flow skills up with fleet-ci-v4 and #1210 (#1215)\n\n## Change\n\nThis is follow-up docs for three PRs that merged today:\nesaueng/remus#1209, esaueng/remus#1210 and esaueng/remus#1212. It is\nthree commits, each kept separate:\n\n1. **Skip-checks trailer.** GitHub skips push and pull_request workflows\nwhen the head commit carries a `skip-checks` trailer, the same as for\nthe bracketed skip markers. The \"No `CI` run at all\" and \"No refresh PR\nopened\" rows in `pr-workflow/reference.md` now list it. So do the\nmatching troubleshooting row and refresh-mechanics paragraph in\n`release-flow`. Codex raised this on #1209 after #1209 was already\nqueued.\n2. **pr-workflow job catalog for v4.** #1212 activated\n`fleet-ci-v4.yml`, so:\n- \"Hard rules\" in `SKILL.md` and \"CI jobs\" in `reference.md` now name\n`fleet-ci-v4.yml`.\n- The Fuzz Targets Compile and Software Rendering rows no longer say\n\"(tier 2)\".\n3. **Size-declaration collection.** #1210 fixed the case where a commit\ntitle naming an unresolvable PR number aborted collection. The\n`release-flow/SKILL.md` \"Collection is fragile\" note now says it no\nlonger aborts, and names the failures that still leave only the \"Could\nnot collect\" notice: a failed compare or a failed PR-association lookup.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `./scripts/check-doc-paths.sh`: OK.\n- `python3 scripts/check_public_commit_metadata.py --base origin/main\n--head HEAD`: passed.\n- No `fleet-ci-v3.yml` mention remains under `.claude/skills/`.\n- No commit message or line of this description carries a skip marker.\n\n## Compatibility and risks\n\nDocs only. No Rust or workflow changes.\n\n## WASM module tier\n\nNone.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01BvYiTQJWWBACfhhuFhkAxd)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
