          "message": "fix(deps): bump rustls-webpki and webpki-roots past the emSign advisories (#1216)\n\n## Change\n\nTwo RustSec advisories published today make `checks / Cargo Deny` fail\non every PR, including the package refresh esaueng/remus#1214:\n\n- [RUSTSEC-2026-0382](https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0382):\n`rustls-webpki` 0.103.15 can accept certificate paths through distrusted\nemSign intermediates. Fixed in 0.103.16.\n- [RUSTSEC-2026-0381](https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0381):\n`webpki-roots` 1.0.9 bundles `emSign ECC Root CA - G3`. Fixed in 1.0.10.\n\nBoth reach the workspace only through `ureq` in `remus-gauntlet`. This\nis a `Cargo.lock`-only bump of the two packages.\n\nI edited the two entries directly rather than taking `cargo update -p`'s\noutput. That command also re-resolved `tempfile`'s `getrandom` from\n0.4.3 to 0.3.4, which this fix doesn't need.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo check --locked -p remus-gauntlet`: passes, so the edited\nlockfile is consistent with the manifests.\n- `cargo deny` was not run locally (not installed here). The `Cargo\nDeny` job on this PR is the check.\n\n## Compatibility and risks\n\n- Patch-level dependency updates of a tool crate's TLS stack only.\n- No kernel, WASM package, API, format, unit or tolerance change.\n\n## WASM module tier\n\nNone.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_0179reg6tDLuhXn8eRjUjpNn)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
