          "id": "0551bb432abe5b039bf2ee7bdb79e3f57d046f28",
          "message": "fix(ci): date the refresh size span from a squash-merged refresh (#1222)\n\n## Change\n\nThe last two package refresh runs never opened a PR. In both runs, the\n\"Open package refresh PR\" step hit its 15-minute job timeout:\n- [run 484](https://github.com/esaueng/remus/actions/runs/39493536545)\nfor `de63529`;\n- [run 485](https://github.com/esaueng/remus/actions/runs/39502041571)\nfor `e18c10d`.\n\nThe run before them ([run\n483](https://github.com/esaueng/remus/actions/runs/39469824069), which\nopened esaueng/remus#1214) took 14 min 11 s in that step. So the step\nwas slow before it started failing; nothing hung. Meanwhile #1214 is\nstale: it was built from `3fd064e`, and main now includes `27cfb77`. No\nreplacement refresh can be opened until the publisher finishes in time.\n\n**Cause:** `previous_source()` finds the previous refresh by matching\nits commit subject against `REFRESH_SUBJECT`, which expects `… to vX\nfrom <sha>`. Refresh PRs now land squash-merged under their PR title,\n`chore(wasm): refresh committed packages to v2026.1.69 (#1208)`, which\nnames no source. So both #1208 and #1182 were skipped, and the size span\nwas dated from an older refresh. Every refresh then walked every PR\nsince that point, one or two API calls per commit.\n\n**Fix:**\n- `previous_source()` also matches a squash-merged refresh\n(`REFRESH_PR_SUBJECT`). It takes the source from that PR's head branch,\n`codex/wasm-refresh-<40-hex sha>`.\n- `merged_prs()` skips those refresh commits, as it already skips\nsource-style ones.\n- The span in the description prints the first 12 characters of the\nsource sha.\n\nThis PR changes the publisher script, which is in the refresh workflow's\npath filter. Its merge therefore starts a new refresh from that main\nhead. That refresh supersedes esaueng/remus#1214 and should date its\nspan from the #1208 source.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `python3 scripts/test-package-refresh-pr.py`: 12/12 pass.\n- The new test is\n`test_squash_merged_refresh_dates_the_span_from_its_source`. The newest\nrefresh in it is squash-merged, with an older source-style refresh\nbehind it. It checks that the span starts at the squash refresh's\nsource, that the older refresh is never consulted, and that the source\nPR's `WASM-Size:` line is still carried. It fails on `main` without the\nfix.\n- Not run: the real publisher against GitHub, which needs the bot's\ntoken. The merge-triggered refresh run is that check.\n\n## Compatibility and risks\n\n- CI publisher script and its test only.\n- No kernel, package, API, format or workflow change.\n- A refresh PR whose head branch is not the standard\n`codex/wasm-refresh-<sha>` is skipped, so a hand-made refresh still\nfalls back to an older source-style one, as before.\n\n## WASM module tier\n\nNone.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_0179reg6tDLuhXn8eRjUjpNn)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
