          "id": "4985f0aa5b6244c307d0ea9f46c76937697218b6",
          "message": "ci: build up to four merge-queue entries at a time (#1228)\n\n## Change\n\nThe `.github/merge-queue-ruleset.json` template now sets\n`max_entries_to_build` to 4 instead of 2, so the queue validates up to\nfour PRs at once. This came out of the CI review in this session.\nEverything else in the queue rule is unchanged: squash merging,\n`ALLGREEN`, `max_entries_to_merge` 2, minimum 1 entry with no wait, a\n240-minute timeout, no bypass actors, and `\"enforcement\": \"disabled\"` in\nthe template.\n\nFiles that follow the template:\n- `scripts/test-ci-convergence.py` now asserts 4 in\n`test_queue_configuration_preserves_every_merge_validation`.\n- `docs/owner-pr-ci.md` says speculative builds are limited to four.\n- The pr-workflow skill says \"at most four entries built at a time\".\n\n## Verification\n\n- `python3 scripts/test-ci-convergence.py`: 25 tests pass.\n- `./scripts/check-doc-paths.sh` passes, and the JSON parses.\n\n## Compatibility and risks\n\n- **This file is only a template.** The live merge-queue rule doesn't\nread it. After this merges, set **Settings → Rules → the merge-queue\nrule → \"Build concurrency\"** to 4 yourself. Until then the queue keeps\nbuilding 2 entries at a time.\n- **More hosted-runner load.** Each extra entry is a full tier-1 run, so\nthe queue can use up to twice as many runners at once.\n- No Rust, workflow or format changes.\n\n## WASM module tier\n\nNone.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01BvYiTQJWWBACfhhuFhkAxd)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
