          "message": "test(remus): add filleted bracket campaign with ready-repros (#1240)\n\n## Change\n\nAdds `crates/remus/tests/bracket_campaign.rs`. It builds a filleted\nmechanical bracket step by step through the `remus::Model` facade and\nrecords how far the kernel gets, so parallel fillet work has one shared\ntarget. This PR adds tests only; no kernel code changes.\n\n**The part:**\n- A 74×60×4 plate with a U-slot, extruded from its exact profile. The\ntab-fuse-then-slot order is avoided because it mesh-falls-back until\n#1237 lands.\n- Two 18×10×40 tabs, fused.\n- Cuts: a groove, a counterbored hole, two countersunk holes and two\ncross holes.\n- Fillet passes F1–F7, selecting edges by endpoint predicates.\n\n**Passing steps (13 tests).** Each is checked for:\n- exact boolean quality and zero NURBS faces\n- `validate` valid\n- a watertight welded mesh\n- volume change against a closed form:\n  - vertical corners: `T·r²(1−π/4)`\n  - concave F2: material added\n- F5 corners: `Σ(L−2r)·r²(1−π/4) + 8r³(1−π/6)`. The rolling-ball\ntwo-edge corner is a ball octant plus a planar ledge\n(`build_two_edge_corner_exact`), not a mitre.\n  - holes and countersinks: cylinder and frustum volumes\n\n**Ready-repros (10 `#[ignore]` tests).** Each asserts the desired\nresult:\n\n| Test | Today's refusal |\n|---|---|\n| `f4_concave_tab_base_edges_alone` | postcondition: 16 free edges, 1\ninconsistent orientation |\n| `sequence_f3_after_f1_f2` | postcondition: 11 free edges, 1\ninconsistent orientation (F3 alone passes) |\n| `sequence_f4_after_f1_f2` | `BlendError::TrimmingFailure` |\n| `sequence_f6_after_f1_f2_f5` | `BlendError::UnsupportedSeamCrossing` |\n| `f7_groove_lips_on_filleted_holed_body` | postcondition: 4\ninconsistent orientations |\n| `f7_groove_lips_after_groove` | same as above, with only the groove\ncut; fails on a single lip edge too (minimal repro) |\n| `f5_tab_top_loops_after_groove` | `UnsupportedVertexBlend { stripes: 2\n}`; the groove alone is enough |\n| `every_edge_r0_5` / `_r1` / `_r2` | `UnsupportedVertexBlend { stripes:\n2 }` |\n\n`current_refusals_are_typed_and_atomic` pins these refusal codes. It\nalso checks that every refusal leaves its input body valid and\nunchanged. When a fix lands, drop its row there and un-ignore its repro.\n\n`f3_after_groove_refuses_with_cliff` asserts a correct refusal, not a\ngap. The groove leaves only 1.5 mm of tab wall, so an r2 fillet has\nnowhere to land (`CliffEncountered`, available radius 1.5).\n\n**Differences from the brief:**\n- F2 after the cuts **passes** on `main` (F1 then F2 on the fully cut\nbody). It is asserted as a passing step.\n- Every-edge r2 on the *cut* body fails with a cliff (available radius\n1.8), not a 2-stripe blend. The every-edge repros use the uncut tabbed\nbody, where all three radii give the 2-stripe refusal.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo test --profile ci-test -p remus --test bracket_campaign`: 13\npassed, 10 ignored, 3.2 s.\n- `-- --ignored`: all 10 fail at the intended fillet refusal, not at an\nearlier oracle.\n- `cargo clippy -p remus --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`: clean.\n- `./scripts/check-doc-paths.sh`: passes.\n\n## Compatibility and risks\n\nNone. This adds a test file only. The test reads\n`remus_topology::explorer` and `FaceSurface`, which are already\ndependencies of `remus`.\n\n## WASM module tier\n\nNone.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01LJdrafe1GyfqLL44PXL8Sm)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
