          "id": "1f7c64db2c5c31064e6fc7a896917fa95dd823eb",
          "message": "fix(fillet): make rolling-ball fillet output deterministic across processes (#1242)\n\n## Change\n\n`crates/operations/src/fillet/{rolling_ball,mod,helpers}.rs` built their\nadjacency, setback, contact-point and corner tables from std\n`HashMap`/`HashSet`. Their per-process random seed reached iteration\norder, so the same fillet came back with a different face order and\ndifferent arena bytes in each process.\n\n**Confirmed before the fix:** 12 edges of a 20×10×40 box at r2 (rolling\nball, and `fillet_v2`, which takes the same path on this box) plus an\nL-bracket wall-top rim at r1.5. Arenas serialized in separate processes\nhad the same length and different bytes every time.\n\n**Fix:** the three files now alias `DetHashMap`/`DetHashSet` (`use\nremus_math::det_hash::{DetHashMap as HashMap, …}`), following the\npattern in `boolean/mod.rs`. `::new()` becomes `::default()` and\n`with_capacity(n)` becomes `with_capacity_and_hasher(n, DetState)`. The\nthree files are removed from `scripts/det-hash-grandfather.txt`.\nIteration order is now fixed across processes. It is not sorted, so no\nexisting output order is reworked. That keeps the diff mechanical while\nother fillet work is in flight.\n\nOut of scope: `remus-blend`'s `fillet_builder.rs`/`chamfer_builder.rs`\nand `operations/src/blend_ops.rs` are still grandfathered. The cases\nabove don't reach their hash-order paths.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New `crates/operations/tests/fillet_determinism.rs`: re-runs its own\ntest binary as 4 worker processes per case and requires byte-identical\n`arena_io::serialize_solid` output against the parent. Before the fix it\n**fails** on all three cases. After it passes, repeated 4×.\n- `cargo test -p remus-operations fillet`: 201 passed, 0 failed. `--test\nblend_integration` passes, and so does `remus-io --test\nfillet_preserves_input`.\n- `cargo clippy -p remus-operations --all-targets -D warnings` and\n`cargo fmt --check` are clean.\n- `scripts/check-det-hash.sh`: OK (51 files grandfathered).\n- `scripts/check-approx-census.py`: matches all 52 committed rows.\n- Perf: see the comment below (criterion `box+fillet` benches, main vs\nbranch).\n\n## Compatibility and risks\n\nNo API, format, unit or tolerance changes. Fillet face order (and so the\narena bytes) is now fixed, but it differs from whatever order a given\nprocess produced before. Anything that pinned one seed's output would\nsee a one-time change. No goldens changed.\n\n## WASM module tier\n\nNone\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01RLR7G7BCksDxEwSEgQV5Mx)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
