          "id": "64394e9058205d0b89b0dc2ccfcdc9de51d2df99",
          "message": "feat(roadmap): conflict-free roadmap evidence fragments (#1258)\n\n## Change\n\nOn 2026-10-21, 17 of the 23 open PRs edited\n`docs/kernel-maturity/roadmap.md`. Its rows are single-line table cells,\nso each merge left the rest of those PRs conflicted.\n\n- **Evidence fragments.** A PR now records its evidence in\n`docs/kernel-maturity/roadmap-evidence/<row>--<slug>.md` instead of\nediting the row. The front matter has `row` and an optional `state`; see\nthe README in that directory.\n- `python3 scripts/roadmap-evidence.py` checks the fragments against the\nroadmap.\n- `--fold` appends them to their rows in a standalone `docs(roadmap):\nfold evidence` PR and deletes the files.\n- A fragment is refused if its row is unknown or ambiguous, or if a\nsecond fragment also sets the same row's state.\n  - Untouched rows stay byte-identical.\n- Text never goes into the PERF `Priority / phase / evidence` column,\nwhich `sync-roadmap-inventory.py` parses. PERF rows receive it in their\nState column.\n- **Roadmap header and session workflow step 4** now point to fragments.\n- **Separate fix: four blank lines inside the bridge register.** They\nended the Markdown table after B10, B28, B75 and B260. GitHub rendered\nB11 onward in each following block as plain paragraphs.\n\n**Agent-guide changes, approved by the owner on 2026-10-22:**\n- `AGENTS.md` (Delivery): a session may arm auto-merge on a PR it opened\nonce that PR is green on its exact head, has no conflict, and every\nreview thread is answered and resolved, unless the PR carries the `hold`\nlabel.\n- `.claude/skills/pr-workflow/SKILL.md`: records that the Codex bot\nposts blocking inline P1/P2 threads; makes answering and resolving them\nstep 3 of the merge gate; documents the REST routes\n(`ccr/review_threads`, `ccr/comments/<id>/resolve`, `ccr/auto_merge`)\nfor cloud sessions without GraphQL; adds the standing auto-merge rule.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `python3 scripts/test-roadmap-evidence.py`: 12 tests OK. The tests\ncover parsing and refusals, escaped and code-span pipes, the\nevidence-column choice, the PERF code column, file-name ordering,\ncompeting state changes, and fold-and-delete. They also fold one\nfragment into each of the 369 anchored rows of the real roadmap at once.\nBefore the blank-line fix, 130 of those rows were not reachable.\n- `python3 scripts/roadmap-evidence.py`: 0 fragments, passes.\n- `python3 scripts/sync-roadmap-inventory.py --check`: passes, also\nafter a trial fold that set a PERF row's state and appended evidence.\n- `./scripts/check-doc-paths.sh`: passes.\n- Not run: Rust builds and tests, because no Rust code changed.\n`test-roadmap-evidence.py` is not wired into CI. Adding it means staging\na new `fleet-ci` version, which is left as a follow-up.\n\n## Compatibility and risks\n\n- Process change: new PRs record evidence in fragments. Open PRs that\nalready edit rows directly keep working.\n- No public API, file format, unit, tolerance, dependency or WASM\npackage changes.\n\n## WASM module tier\n\nNone.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01RQdpS6MhmR3YaBbbXWybVv)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
