          "id": "817ea9fc8547f0ad2d131b19f8012a88ecec0b55",
          "message": "fix(kernel): integrate NURBS and 3MF repairs with paired WASM 2026.1.75 (#1257)\n\nCombine the 3MF repair from #1255, NURBS numeric checks from #1256 and\nallocation-free borrowed validation from #1257, then ship the kernel and\ntranslator together at **2026.1.75** after the fillet and offset\nintegrations. All seven original math/3MF source files and their\nregressions are preserved.\n\nThe 3MF reader treats unsupported extension subtrees as opaque and\naccepts geometry and placement elements only directly under their core\nparents. NURBS validation preserves error order, payloads, caches and\nnumeric behavior while handling extreme inputs and reading existing\ncontrol-point, knot and weight storage without temporary copies.\n\nThe paired packages were generated by the normal optimized `cargo xtask\nwasm-build` on Linux from public source\n`8d2dc2df89e808ac69cbf9e076b740d2350dd4dd`, using default in-checkout\ntargets, Rust/Cargo 1.96.0, wasm-pack 0.15.0, wasm-bindgen 0.2.126 and\nwasm-opt 117. Generated-only commit\n`77f7122a8c81ca43e095d0890a835fc17095d608` changes five files across the\ntwo complete package directories: both manifests, both WASM modules and\nthe kernel raw WASM declaration. All 2,178 non-generated tracked files\nremain byte-identical to that source. Both package versions are\n2026.1.75, and repository/homepage metadata follows the normal\ncommitted-snapshot publisher. No registry publication or release is\nincluded.\n\nThe previous .74 snapshot failed the clean Ubuntu rebuild comparison for\nboth WASM modules and the kernel raw declaration. This Linux\nregeneration retains the integrity guard unchanged; the precise cause of\nthe earlier host difference remains unproven. Independent hosted byte\nreproduction passed on this exact head in run39862629314 attempt1.\nCurrent-head platform qualification run39866098779 attempt1 passed all\nsix standard hosts: Ubuntu x64/ARM64, Mac Intel/ARM64 and Windows\nx64/ARM64. Each artifact was independently bound to the provider\nrun/job/head, archive digest, all20 committed package hashes and actual\nnative OS/compiler/runtime identity. All439 required gates per host and\nall36 advisory records are retained, including the four known\ndirect/batch gaps.\n\nValidation:\n\n- The normal Linux optimized xtask completed successfully, including\npackage metadata/export/type/size checks, the full direct smoke suite\nand actual installed-tarball consumer regressions. Both complete\ngenerated directories retain all 20 tracked files, including the raw\ndeclarations, license and notice.\n- Prior-head six-host qualification at\n`8d2dc2df89e808ac69cbf9e076b740d2350dd4dd` passed 439 required gates per\nhost, retaining all 36 advisories and the four known direct/batch gaps.\nThat evidence remains attributed to its .74 distribution; it is not a\n.75 package qualification.\n- Separate source qualification recorded strict all-target/all-feature\nworkspace Clippy passing and native tests at **9,053 passed, one pinned\nmesh-digest failure and 36 skipped**. The unchanged assertion and\nexactly the same four actual digests reproduce on untouched main. Its\nplatform cause remains unproven; no assertion or tolerance was relaxed.\nNative workspace validation is not all-pass.\n- Doctests, complexity guards, roadmap evidence, all 22 repository\npolicy checks and the complete approximation census passed separately.\nThe ignored G1-chain campaign remains unqualified.\n\nMeasured against the packages committed at PR base\n`77ee1facb78244ca7e8b19f40f31dc2a358a77da`: kernel raw 10,493,298 →\n10,619,675 bytes; gzip 3,885,910 → 3,938,898; Brotli q11 2,765,478 →\n2,800,823, using the base revision's repository policy script with Node\n24.14.0. All hard limits pass without warnings. Translator raw 3,086,386\n→ 3,142,363 bytes.\n\nWASM-Size: +126377 bytes raw, combined exact fillet and offset history\nwith NURBS validation, Tier: core (updates session handles and the\njournal)\n\nHosted required checks, reviews, final source parity and each protected\nmerge-group candidate must pass before merge. The consumer pin advances\nthrough OpenZCAD's normal updater after the paired package commit lands;\nits existing automatic deployment accompanies that consumer merge.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: petertoday <171875562+petertoday@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
