          "id": "1325e1918c09ecc1972aac7c3087daca4c1a584d",
          "message": "feat(sweep): qualify tapered polygonal profiles with holes (#1327)\n\nScale laws now resize every outer and inner boundary about the same\nouter-profile center, producing the intended tapered hollow polygon\ninstead of an unscaled bore. The repair also normalizes newly\nconstructed hole winding, honors dimensionless scale changes smaller\nthan linear tolerance, and prevents exactly collinear rounded tangents\nfrom collapsing small translated sections. Malformed scale arrays now\nrefuse transactionally instead of silently selecting unit scale.\n\nThe qualified family is affinely parameterized straight +Z paths with\nnative spine domain [0,1], planar XY straight-edge profiles with polygon\nholes, fixed contact and linear or section-aligned piecewise-linear\nscale laws, across three scales and translated placement. General curved\nboundaries/paths, twist and continuous nonlinear error bounds remain\noutside this increment.\n\nValidation: three native qualification tests cover 24 annular-taper\nmatrix cells, one asymmetric eccentric-hole cell and actual-ring\nrollback; three WASM binding contracts passed. Existing sweep tests\npassed 64/64, B12 4/4 and B124 6/6. All 52 semantic approximation-census\nrows matched under the feature-unified ci-test configuration. Normal\nall-target/all-feature workspace hooks, documentation/module-map,\nroadmap and Git privacy checks passed. The committed package\nindependently reproduces the original volume 200 versus expected 168.\nCanonical optimized dual-package build, full fresh smoke and\ninstalled-tarball suites passed at production source 25886d689. All 72\ntaper cells passed per package suite and in a separate retained\nnpm-installed consumer; all eight published files in each package\nmatched generated bytes and modes. Kernel growth is 1,658 raw bytes. The\ncurrent qualification follow-up changes only tests and documentation,\nwith an empty production/build-input diff; hosted CI on that final head\nis still running. No dependencies or committed packages changed.\n\nWASM-Size: tapered hollow polygonal sweeps, Tier: core (builds and\ncommits live-session topology).",
          "timestamp": "2026-10-28T22:18:05Z",
