          "id": "380a4acf000339076e9aa4f662d0c36d81e9775a",
          "message": "fix(algo): orient internal helical gear rings by their trimmed flux (#1470)\n\n## Change\n\n`cut_gear_teeth` refused internal helical teeth in a bore once the face\nwidth passed about 5 mm, for example 40 teeth at 15° helix over a 7 or\n10 mm bore. The exact fuse built the right faces into one closed shell,\nbut shell assembly classified that shell as a hole and failed with \"no\nouter shell found (all shells classified as holes)\".\n\nFor a lone shell, the hole test falls back to an outward-flux sum, ∮ P·n\ndA. It integrated each curved face over the (u, v) box of its boundary.\nAn internal helical gear's tip and root lands face the axis and are\nhelical strips on cylinders, and each strip's box spans its whole twist.\nTheir negative flux was overcounted roughly in proportion to width²,\nwhile the caps grow linearly with width, so past some width the sum\nturned negative. The trace on the 7 mm case:\n\n| Faces | Flux |\n|---|---:|\n| reversed lands, as counted | −63,000 |\n| reversed lands, true value | about −8,000 |\n| whole shell | −20,186 |\n\nNow a cylinder or cone face bounded by a single wire that does not wind\naround the axis integrates only the grid cells inside its boundary\npolygon in (u, v), with u unwrapped across the seam. Every other face,\nincluding full-turn bands and faces with inner wires, keeps the box as\nbefore.\n\n## Verification\n\n- **New regression**,\n`gear/cylinder/tests.rs::internal_helical_teeth_in_a_bore_match_the_standalone_gear`.\nCases, all 40 teeth at 15° helix:\n  - right hand, whole 7 mm bore;\n  - left hand, whole 10 mm bore;\n  - left hand over z 1..8 of a 9 mm bore.\n\nEach result must be valid and watertight, and match the closed form\nwithin 1e-9 relative: the ring less the hole growth over the span, with\nthe transverse outline area from a boolean-free standalone gear.\nMeasured errors are under 2e-13.\n- **Also checked:** a probe with 25° helix over a whole 12 mm bore\nbuilds within 1e-14.\n- **Local runs:**\n- all 76 `gear::` tests, all 802 `remus-algo` lib tests and 282\n`remus-operations` boolean tests pass;\n  - fmt and the wildcard-arm ratchet pass;\n- `cargo clippy -p remus-algo -p remus-operations --all-targets -D\nwarnings` passes.\n\n## Compatibility and risks\n\n- No public API change.\n- **Behaviour change in shared code:** the outward-flux test that\ndecides growth against hole shells now trims single-wire, non-winding\ncylinder and cone faces to their boundary. It is consulted only when a\nshell's corner-fan signed volume reads negative.\n- **Still refused, separate defects, not changed here:**\n- internal herringbone teeth: the fuse leaves non-manifold edges, or a\ndisconnected shell over a partial span;\n- 30 teeth at 20° helix over z 3..6 of a 9 mm bore: the fuse leaves 12\nfree edges.\n\n## WASM module tier\n\nWASM-Size: about +1 KiB raw for this change, the trimmed flux in the\nexisting GFA shell assembly, Tier: core (booleans edit the live\nsession's solids). The committed package is still v2026.1.97, so the CI\ntotal also includes earlier merges' growth: esaueng/remus#1456's +78\nKiB, plus esaueng/remus#1461, esaueng/remus#1466 and esaueng/remus#1469.\nesaueng/remus#1460 refreshes the package.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_013o777395iN2GjbBXkAcEfv)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
